s.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-03-22T09:06:35Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T03:24:47Z","body":"**Robert Buchholz ([@rbuchholz](https://github.com/rbuchholz)) wrote:**\n\nI tend to agree with the caution regarding the use of dots in identifiers, thank you for the insight. Maybe $ is a better option, on the other hand it moves the strict quoting requirement from SQL to Shell scripts operating on databases. \n\nI've tried ``quoted_name`` for a workaround, but it did not work. For now, I'm using this (a bit whacky) version:\n```\ndef workaround_alembic_487(name):\n    from pkg_resources import parse_version\n    # Alembic before 0.9.9 did not quote constraint names\n    # https://bitbucket.org/zzzeek/alembic/issues/487/drop_constraint-does-not-quote-check\n    if parse_version(alembic.__version__) <= parse_version('0.9.8'):\n        return \"`%s`\" % name\n    return name\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441887707/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"ey